      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It’s not patronizing—it’s practical, because even if the universe is silent, your nervous system still feels pain, and kindness is just a way to reduce that suffering. Accepting the nothingness doesn’t mean giving up; it means letting go of the illusion that you *have* to fight. You can simply exist, drink water, watch the light shift, and let the day pass without demanding it mean something. That’s not pretending—that’s just being alive, and it’s enough.",
